{"id":"fujifilm_provia_400x","name":"Fujifilm Provia 400X","manufacturer":"Fujifilm","kind":"Slide","isBlackAndWhite":false,"source":"Negs","targetPrint":null,"datasheet":{"url":"https://125px.com/docs/film/fuji/Provia_400X_PIB_1007.pdf","title":"Fujichrome Provia 400X, AF3-0213E (2007)"},"credit":"Copyright (c) 2026 Noah Haasis (Negs preparation). Method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Measurement data (c) FUJIFILM Corporation.","license":"Negs film profile, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Prepared with the profile-creation method of spektrafilm by Andrea Volpato (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm; profiles CC BY-SA 4.0, see SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt). Derivatives must credit both, note their modifications and remain CC BY-SA 4.0. Changes: data/CHANGELOG.txt.","dataSource":"Prepared for Negs from the manufacturer's datasheet: FUJICHROME PROVIA 400X Professional [RXP] Fujifilm Product Information Bulletin, Ref. No. AF3-0213E, as published by Fujifilm (no year printed on the curve page), PDF page 7 (spectral sensitivity, per-dye spectral density, characteristic curves; RMS granularity 11). PDF sha256 06204b7e905fabf2c4ad3e77b93008597d85a3d5c51a3f41cd176e1ee919e4c0. Data (c) FUJIFILM Corporation. The curves were read from the PDF's vector paths (tools/film_profiles/extract_pdf.py); the points and axis calibration are in data/profile-sources/fujifilm-reversal/fujifilm_provia_400x/.\nMethod: spektrafilm's public-era profile creator by Andrea Volpato (commit b2c7fe6), its steps for positive films: D-min removed (base synthesised from the curves' D-min), log E zero where green is 0.735 over D-min, Fujifilm's own per-dye spectra scaled so equal amounts view as an 18.4 % neutral under the viewing illuminant, status-A unmixing, a 3 norm_cdfs curve fit, sensitivity balance, densitometer normalisation. Then Negs's steps: sensitivity scaled so an 18.4 % grey gives raw exposure 1 per channel under the reference illuminant, each channel aligned so log E 0 develops its metameric-neutral amount, and spektrafilm's slide grey-ramp refinement run on spektrafilm 28bf883 at data_trustability 1.0. hanatos2025 adaptation window [433.5, 28.3, 606.2, 59.3] fitted on the reflectance corpus (Otsu (https://github.com/enneract/otsu2018), Munsell (https://zenodo.org/records/3269912), human skin (https://www.nist.gov/programs-projects/reflectance-measurements-human-skin), forest colors (https://zenodo.org/records/3269920)) with a weak prior toward the median of spektrafilm's stored windows. Tools and procedure: tools/film_profiles, docs/adding-film-stocks.md D11.\nNegs slide neutralisation (tools/film_profiles/neutralise_positive.py, a Negs step, not spektrafilm's): the red and blue curve models are moved so a grey card filmed at EV -3 to +2.5 and scanned stays neutral, while the status-A densities stay within about 0.10 D (or their deviation before the step, if larger; a soft limit) of the datasheet's characteristic curves, the curves change as little as possible and the DIR pre-correction does not fold; green is not touched. Weights tuned on Provia 100F and tested on Velvia 100, Ektachrome 100 and Kodachrome 64 (data/profile-sources/fujifilm-reversal/calibration/neutralisation_test.json). For this film: grey-ramp neutrality (EV -1 to +2) 0.0316 before, 0.0015 after; largest colour of the ramp C*ab 2.89 before, 2.28 after; largest curve change 0.048 D; worst status-A deviation from the datasheet 0.123 D (before 0.122 D).\nNegs choices: reference illuminant D55 (daylight stock, exposed at 5400 K); viewing illuminant D50; no target print (a slide is viewed or scanned); log_sensitivity_density_over_min 1.0 as printed; spectra left empty (null) outside the published wavelength range; characteristic curves in log10 H as printed; use 'still' and antihalation 'strong' as the shipped spektrafilm Velvia 100 and Provia 100F; DIR couplers: its own table, the class default scaled uniformly so the DIR pre-correction does not fold (D8).","referenceIlluminant":"D55","densitometer":"status_A","densityMinimum":[0.139,0.139,0.139],"wavelengths":[380,385,390,395,400,405,410,415,420,425,430,435,440,445,450,455,460,465,470,475,480,485,490,495,500,505,510,515,520,525,530,535,540,545,550,555,560,565,570,575,580,585,590,595,600,605,610,615,620,625,630,635,640,645,650,655,660,665,670,675,680,685,690,695,700,705,710,715,720,725,730,735,740,745,750,755,760,765,770,775,780],"logSensitivity":[[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,-1.866],[null,null,-1.3493],[null,null,-0.96838],[null,null,-0.70061],[null,null,-0.52961],[null,null,-0.44276],[null,null,-0.40081],[null,null,-0.37747],[null,null,-0.3568],[null,null,-0.31871],[null,null,-0.27493],[null,null,-0.24206],[null,null,-0.24505],[null,null,-0.30395],[null,null,-0.40545],[null,null,-0.53982],[null,null,-0.70085],[null,-1.838,-0.88437],[null,-1.6865,-1.0876],[null,-1.5521,-1.3087],[null,-1.427,-1.547],[null,-1.3086,-1.8034],[null,-1.1958,null],[null,-1.0899,null],[null,-0.99033,null],[null,-0.87518,null],[null,-0.74766,null],[null,-0.6016,null],[null,-0.46586,null],[null,-0.36238,null],[null,-0.29838,null],[null,-0.27724,null],[null,-0.29456,null],[-1.3825,-0.34621,null],[-1.3375,-0.40856,null],[-1.2735,-0.44431,null],[-1.1932,-0.48928,null],[-1.0996,-0.57997,null],[-0.9965,-0.77246,null],[-0.89213,-1.0878,null],[-0.82723,-1.6135,null],[-0.80109,null,null],[-0.77649,null,null],[-0.73901,null,null],[-0.6876,null,null],[-0.62621,null,null],[-0.55761,null,null],[-0.484,null,null],[-0.40773,null,null],[-0.33246,null,null],[-0.2706,null,null],[-0.28163,null,null],[-0.34788,null,null],[-0.45337,null,null],[-0.52163,null,null],[-0.59531,null,null],[-0.67279,null,null],[-0.77566,null,null],[-0.95311,null,null],[-1.1932,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,null,null],[null,nu